<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Bosun (required by notarization).

  Intentionally EMPTY (no exception entitlements). Why nothing is needed:
    - libghostty is *statically* linked into the Bosun Mach-O, not a separate
      dylib, so there is nothing to validate against — `disable-library-validation`
      is unnecessary.
    - The terminal exec's a login shell via posix_spawn, which hardened runtime
      allows without any entitlement.
    - Metal shaders are precompiled at build time (the Metal Toolchain step), so
      no runtime JIT / writable-executable memory is required.

  If a hardened-runtime launch ever faults with a code-signing error (e.g. an
  EXC_BAD_ACCESS in a JIT/W^X path), add the *minimal* exception here and re-test:
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
  Each added key widens the attack surface, so add only what an actual fault proves
  is needed — verified by launching the hardened-runtime-signed app, not by guessing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
